<title>MEXICO: Segcoam completes Asemex merger.</title>
<headline>Segcoam completes Asemex merger.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seguros Comercial America (Segcoam) said it has finished integrating Aseguradora Mexicana (Asemex) into Segcoam's operations after its recent takeover of the firm.</p>
<p>Segcoam said Asemex will be a division that specializes in the public sector. Segcoam itself is a unit of Grupo Pulsar.</p>
<p>Segcoam bought Asemex last May for 955 million pesos, following intervention by the government earlier in the year.</p>
<p>((--Cecilia Cardenas, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728 9552))</p>
